# service nginx start in an Ubuntu container:

The service command checks: "Is systemd running right now?"

It realizes: "No, we are inside a container."

Instead of crashing, it falls back to the legacy method (SysVinit). It looks inside the /etc/init.d/ folder for a plain old bash script named nginx and simply runs it in the background.

your application is PID 1

The PPID (Parent Process ID) is 0. This means the process was started directly by the Docker Engine (the host), not by another process inside the container.

daemon off  -  foreground process         # In container
daemon on   -  background process         # In Server

